  "question": "Ozempic pen: preferred or PA?",
  "status": "answered",
  "assumption": "Assuming NY Medicaid (NYRx PDL), since the program wasn't named.",
  "answer": "Assuming NY Medicaid: **Ozempic pen is preferred** on the NYRx PDL (revised 9/14/2026), in the GLP-1 RA Type 2 Diabetes class. It has no 10/22/2026 change marker, so the status holds today (10/14/2026).\n\n- The class carries clinical criteria (CC). Confirm an FDA-approved or compendia-supported indication that Medicaid covers.\n- PA is required if the patient is on a GLP-1 and a DPP-IV inhibitor concurrently.\n- Ozempic **tablets**, Rybelsus, Mounjaro, Soliqua, Xultophy and generic liraglutide are non-preferred.\n\nThe PDL doesn't spell out the PA process for preferred GLP-1s beyond these criteria.",
